const BUILD_V = "0.18.0", CHANGELOG = [{"v": "0.18.0", "d": "2026-11-25", "n": ["Four new energy makers, tiers 11 to 14: Fractal Lattice, Mirror Loom, Dream Engine and Genesis Forge. Each one shows up when you unlock its world and makes about 1,000 times more than the tier before it", "25 new upgrades: five tree upgrades for each new maker, Fabricator IV to autobuy them, and four Flux upgrades for very late runs (Flux Recursion, Reflection, Reverie and Genesis)", "20 new achievements for owning the new makers"]}, {"v": "0.17.0", "d": "2026-11-25", "n": ["New in the story: four chapters about the worlds past the multiverse, right after After the Wall, with four new characters: Facet the crystal, Alev (Vela's reflection), Morrow the sleepy dreamer and Lumen, the first light", "Already past that point? The new chapters count as done and their rewards are yours. Watch them in Crew \u203a Story", "The new worlds pay out a lot more: Fractal, Mirror, Dream and Origin now each multiply all your energy production, and the deeper the world, the bigger the boost", "Fixed: Watch the ending again played the wrong chapter, and the chapter reward line said \u00d72 when it gives \u00d71.5"]}, {"v": "0.16.0", "d": "2026-11-25", "n": ["Four new dimensions past the multiverse: Fractal, Mirror, Dream and Origin, each with its own twist. Find them after Infinite in Worlds", "Every dimension now has its own sky, not just a new colour: a crystal lattice, a rising sun, a solar system, star-forming pillars, a black hole that swallows stars, a galaxy inside a clock, a day and night with a real sun and moon, bubble universes, a fractal, a mirror lake, a dream sky and the first light", "Your engine turns into each new world too, with its own picture"]}, {"v": "0.15.0", "d": "2026-11-25", "n": ["Buy buttons you can't afford yet show how long until you can, like \"in 42s\". Upgrades show it too when you tap them", "The Prestige screen says how long until you can reset. Once you can, it shows how much you're earning per minute, so you can tell when it's worth resetting", "On small phones like the iPhone SE, currencies sit in one row you can swipe, so the top bar takes less room", "Fixed: the upgrade tree's \"owned\" count was hard to read over the tree"]}, {"v": "0.14.1", "d": "2026-11-25", "n": ["Easier to get on iPhone: open the game's link in Safari and it shows you how to add it to your home screen. Stats \u203a Settings has an iPhone section with the steps too"]}, {"v": "0.14.0", "d": "2026-11-24", "n": ["The game has a new name, Ten Cells, and its own icon: ten glowing cells around a bright core. Your save carries over as it is", "Screen size setting for PC (Stats \u203a Settings): Auto fills a big screen, or pick 100\u2013200%. The + and \u2212 keys change it too. The PC app also has window size presets", "PC app save file moved to Documents \u203a Ten Cells. A save in the old Infinity Engine folder is still found and brought across", "Fixed: an egg from beating a boss or finishing a chapter was lost if the incubator already had 3 eggs. Those eggs now always arrive, even past 3"]}, {"v": "0.13.0", "d": "2026-11-24", "n": ["Three new story characters: Juno the courier pilot, Bram the stardust miner and Echo, a hologram of a lost builder, each with a 3D model and their own scenes", "Your reactor grows: every world you unlock replaces the atom with something bigger, from a molecule to the whole multiverse", "The space background takes on the colour of your newest world", "Worlds now say exactly how to unlock them: a checklist with progress on every locked world, and the next one is highlighted"]}, {"v": "0.12.0", "d": "2026-11-24", "n": ["Generator cards show how long until you can afford the next one", "Buy everything: one button buys the max of every generator", "Next goal on the Engine screen: your current story mission and its progress. Tap it to open the story", "Keyboard shortcuts on PC: Space taps, 1 to 6 switch tabs, G buys everything, U buys upgrades, A fires abilities, M mutes, F goes full screen. The list is in Settings", "Stats has a graph of your energy per second over the last two hours", "New Log tab in Stats: every notification with its time, so nothing gets missed"]}, {"v": "0.11.0", "d": "2026-11-24", "n": ["Install it as a PC app from the Claude desktop app (Stats \u203a Settings \u203a PC app): its own window and icon, and full screen with F11", "The PC app keeps your save in a file on your computer (Documents \u203a Infinity Engine \u203a save.txt), checks it every time it starts, and carries it over to every update, with a backup of each older version"]}, {"v": "0.10.2", "d": "2026-11-24", "n": ["Numbers are much easier to read: digits use a clearer retro font with more space between them, so 3, 8 and 9 no longer blur together", "The upgrade tree is a spiral galaxy now: every branch curls out from the core along curved links", "New loading screen: a hyperspace starfield, a spinning pixel atom, a waving title, a progress percentage and tips"]}, {"v": "0.10.1", "d": "2026-11-24", "n": ["The upgrade tree is now a circle: every branch is a wedge around the core, with round upgrades on even rings", "Upgrades you don't own yet are easier to see, and the tree opens zoomed in on the core", "Every chapter now has a middle scene that unlocks halfway through its missions, and the first story chapters have longer openings and endings", "The main story up to Infinity (chapters 1 to 24) now lasts about a week if you play around 2 hours a day. Chapters 25 to 38 are the long endgame", "Fixed: tapping an artifact you hadn't found yet showed 'undefined'", "If you were mid-story, your time already played counts toward the new chapter goals"]}, {"v": "0.10.0", "d": "2026-11-24", "n": ["The story is three times longer: 38 chapters instead of 12, a new character called Sable, and three chapters after the ending", "10 new bosses past Infinity, each a new 3D monster. They appear once you break Infinity", "45 new upgrades: 26 in the upgrade tree, 3 Fragment perks, more Singularity, Ascension and Void upgrades, and 10 Ultra upgrades including two for after the Omega Engine", "Balance: the long stall before Infinity is gone, early bosses are spaced out instead of all dying in the first ten minutes, Break Infinity is cheaper and your first Ultra climb is faster than your first normal climb", "Story chapters now give \u00d71.5 production each. Your place in the story is kept, and the new chapters before it count as done", "Smoother on phones: 3D models and the prestige portal redraw at 30 fps and skip work when they're off screen"]}, {"v": "0.9.0", "d": "2026-11-24", "n": ["New Crew tab: a 12-chapter story with talking 3D characters, plus 3D pets that hatch from eggs, level up and evolve", "Your active pet hangs out next to the reactor on the Engine screen. Tap it", "Ultra Prestige: a new final layer that wipes everything for Ultra Points and 25 Ultra upgrades. Build the Omega Engine to beat the game", "The full game now takes about a year to finish", "36 more badges (180 in total) and new Ultra achievements", "Nicer celebration banner for evolutions, boss kills and big badges", "Fixed the space background sometimes not showing"]}, {"v": "0.8.0", "d": "2026-11-24", "n": ["The Prestige tab is now a portal: all six layers sit around a glowing ring that fills up as you get close to your next prestige", "Update notices: the game tells you when a new version is out, and one tap updates it with your save kept", "Auto-prestige shows a quick note instead of replaying the full animation every time", "Notifications sit under the top bar so they no longer cover buttons or your energy", "Long hint text wraps instead of getting cut off"]}, {"v": "0.7.0", "d": "2026-11-24", "n": ["Loading screen and a short terms page on first launch", "Bosses are now animated 3D monsters that flinch when you hit them", "New prestige animation: collapse, white-out, shockwave", "Badges: 90 medals across 18 tracks, +2% production each", "New slow lo-fi space soundtrack and softer click sounds", "The upgrade tree is now a web that spreads out from the core"]}];
